# RISK-BUDGET FIX (report-driven). This was 50. A system whose last measured
# window ran a 30.2% win rate at profit factor 0.17 must not be told "you may
# take 50 trades" -- at that expectancy, permission to trade 50 times is
# permission to lose 50 times. The count limit is now a backstop, not the
# governing control: what actually governs entries is INTRADAY_DAILY_RISK_BUDGET_PCT
# below ("you have a limited risk budget; spend it only on the best positive-EV
# opportunities"). Lowering the count alone would have been cosmetic -- the
# budget is the real change, and the count is simply no longer absurd.
INTRADAY_MAX_TRADES_PER_DAY = int(os.environ.get('INTRADAY_MAX_TRADES_PER_DAY', '8'))
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTRADAY RISK BUDGET (replaces "you may take N trades" as the governing rule)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A trade's cost to the account is not 1 unit of a trade quota -- it is
# (entry - stop) * quantity, in rupees, at risk. Two trades can differ by 4x in
# what they can actually lose while counting identically against a trade cap,
# which is why a trade cap is the wrong instrument for controlling risk.
#
# The budget model: each day starts with DAILY_RISK_BUDGET_PCT of capital as
# money the account is willing to lose. Every entry reserves its own risk amount
# from that budget, and when the budget is gone the day is over regardless of how
# many trades that took -- one trade or eight. MAX_CONCURRENT_RISK_PCT separately
# caps how much of it may be exposed at the same moment, so the whole day's budget
# cannot be lost in one simultaneous cluster of correlated positions.
#
# RESERVE_PCT is what makes the budget selective rather than first-come-first-
# served: once that share of the budget has been spent, the remaining risk is
# released only to candidates with a materially better expected edge than the
# ones already taken. Otherwise a budget behaves exactly like a trade quota --
# the first N signals of the morning take everything and the best setup of the
# day arrives to an empty account.
INTRADAY_RISK_BUDGET_ENABLED = os.environ.get('INTRADAY_RISK_BUDGET_ENABLED', 'true').lower() != 'false'
INTRADAY_DAILY_RISK_BUDGET_PCT = float(os.environ.get('INTRADAY_DAILY_RISK_BUDGET_PCT', '2.0'))
INTRADAY_MAX_CONCURRENT_RISK_PCT = float(os.environ.get('INTRADAY_MAX_CONCURRENT_RISK_PCT', '1.0'))
INTRADAY_RISK_BUDGET_RESERVE_PCT = float(os.environ.get('INTRADAY_RISK_BUDGET_RESERVE_PCT', '40'))
# Minimum context-adjusted expected NET edge (% per trade) a proven candidate must
# clear to be worth any of the budget at all. 0.0 = "must be positive after costs".
INTRADAY_MIN_EV_PCT_TO_TRADE = float(os.environ.get('INTRADAY_MIN_EV_PCT_TO_TRADE', '0.0'))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
